  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "An array BBB is called good if the prefix XOR array is non-decreasing. Formally, the following condition should hold:\n\n\nFor all 1≤i&lt;j≤∣B∣1 \\le i &lt; j \\le |B|1≤i&lt;j≤∣B∣, B1⊕B2⊕....⊕Bi≤B1⊕B2⊕...⊕BjB_1 \\oplus B_2 \\oplus .... \\oplus B_i \\le B_1 \\oplus B_2 \\oplus ... \\oplus B_jB1​⊕B2​⊕....⊕Bi​≤B1​⊕B2​⊕...⊕Bj​.\nYou are given an array AAA with NNN integers, and need to answer QQQ queries of the following form:\n\n\nGiven LLL and RRR, is A[L,R]A[L, R]A[L,R] good where A[L,R]A[L, R]A[L,R] represents the subarray [AL,AL+1,...,AR][A_L, A_{L + 1}, ..., A_R][AL​,AL+1​,...,AR​].\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains 222 integers - NNN and QQQ, the size of the array and the number of queries.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​.\nThe next QQQ lines contain 222 integers each - LLL and RRR, representing a query.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a binary string SSS of length QQQ, where Si=1S_i = 1Si​=1 if the subarray in the iii-th query is good, else Si=0S_i = 0Si​=0.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N,Q≤2⋅1051 \\le N, Q \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N,Q≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai≤1090 \\le A_i \\le 10^90≤Ai​≤109",
      "1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of QQQ does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
